{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on request 8022a296, for S6: the deferral stands, and the\nseverity does not change. The custody page states the limits as you\nfound them.\n\n1. A consumed invitation admits no other key. The retained secret\n   reveals no private seed and gives no authority of the admitted\n   member.\n2. The one remaining use needs an authorized issuer to give the same\n   `inviteHash` to another invitation that is still open. That issuer\n   can already invite any key. The CLI makes a fresh random secret for\n   each invitation, so the reuse does not happen by the ordinary path.\n3. Write the paragraph with those two facts and the two file names of\n   your source note. Do not claim that reuse has happened or that it\n   cannot.\n\nNo uniqueness guard on `inviteHash` is filed. A guard is a Membership\nchange, and it would need a new creation family for a case that only\nan authorized issuer can cause.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}